<h2 class="wp-block-heading">TV Mounting Height FAQ</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How high should a TV be mounted from the floor?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mount the TV so the center of the screen is at the seated eye level of the main viewer, which is often around 42 inches (107 cm) from the floor for a standard sofa. A 55 inch TV centered there has its bottom edge about 29 inches up and its top edge about 55 inches up.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Where should the center of a TV be?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The center of the screen should line up with your eyes when you sit where you usually watch. If that is not possible, keep the angle from your eyes up to the center of the screen under 15 degrees, which CE Pro and THX guidance treat as the limit for comfortable viewing.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Is a TV above a fireplace too high?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Often, yes. A mantel usually pushes the center of the screen well above seated eye level, and the viewing angle can go past 15 degrees. Use the fireplace option in the calculator to check the real angle, and consider a pull-down mount, sitting further back or another wall.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How high should a TV be in a bedroom?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A bedroom TV usually goes a little higher than a living room TV because you sit higher in bed. Sit up the way you normally watch, measure from the floor to your eyes and put the center of the screen at that height, or slightly above if you lean back on pillows.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">More Planning Tools</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Planning the rest of the room? Try our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/rug-size-calculator/">rug size calculator</a>, <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/curtain-size-calculator/">curtain size calculator</a> and <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/shelf-spacing-calculator/">shelf spacing calculator</a>, or get ideas for the console under the TV in our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/coffee-table-decor/">coffee table decor</a> guide.</p>



